ளி","parts":[{"text":"அம்","lemma":"am","gloss":"sweet/beautiful"},{"text":"புளி","lemma":"puḷi","gloss":"sour"}],"gloss":"sweet and sour"},{"surface":"மிதவை","parts":[{"text":"மிதவை","lemma":"mitavai","gloss":"porridge"}],"gloss":"porridge"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அவரை","parts":[{"text":"அவரை","lemma":"avarai","gloss":"field beans"}],"gloss":"field beans"},{"surface":"கொய்யுநர்","parts":[{"text":"கொய்","lemma":"koy","gloss":"pluck"},{"text":"உநர்","lemma":"uṉar","gloss":"they who do"}],"gloss":"those who pluck"},{"surface":"ஆர","parts":[{"text":"ஆர","lemma":"āra","gloss":"to fullness"}],"gloss":"to their fill"},{"surface":"மாந்தும்","parts":[{"text":"மாந்தும்","lemma":"māntum","gloss":"eating"}],"gloss":"eating"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"தென்னம்","parts":[{"text":"தென்","lemma":"teṉ","gloss":"southern"},{"text":"அம்","lemma":"am","gloss":"euphonic increment"}],"gloss":"southern"},{"surface":"பொருப்பன்","parts":[{"text":"பொருப்பன்","lemma":"poruppaṉ","gloss":"lord of the hills"}],"gloss":"lord of the hills"},{"surface":"நன்னாட்டு","parts":[{"text":"நல்","lemma":"nal","gloss":"good"},{"text":"நாட்டு","lemma":"nāṭṭu","gloss":"land (oblique)"}],"gloss":"good country"},{"surface":"உள்ளும்","parts":[{"text":"உள்","lemma":"uḷ","gloss":"inside"},{"text":"உம்","lemma":"um","gloss":"even/also"}],"gloss":"even within"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"பிசிரோன்","parts":[{"text":"பிசிர்","lemma":"picir","gloss":"Pisir (village)"},{"text":"ஓன்","lemma":"ōṉ","gloss":"he of"}],"gloss":"he of Pisir"},{"surface":"என்ப","parts":[{"text":"என்ப","lemma":"eṉpa","gloss":"they say"}],"gloss":"they say"},{"surface":"என்","parts":[{"text":"என்","lemma":"eṉ","gloss":"my"}],"gloss":"my"},{"surface":"உயிர்","parts":[{"text":"உயிர்","lemma":"uyir","gloss":"life"}],"gloss":"life"},{"surface":"ஓம்புநனே","parts":[{"text":"ஓம்புநன்","lemma":"ōmpuṉaṉ","gloss":"protector"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"indeed"}],"gloss":"indeed the protector"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"செல்வ்க்","parts":[{"text":"செல்வ்க்","lemma":"selva","gloss":"wealthy"}],"gloss":"wealthy"},{"surface":"காலை","parts":[{"text":"காலை","lemma":"kālai","gloss":"time"}],"gloss":"time"},{"surface":"நிற்பினும்","parts":[{"text":"நிற்பினும்","lemma":"niṟpiṉum","gloss":"even if standing/present"}],"gloss":"even if present"}]},{"words":[{"surface":"அல்லற்","parts":[{"text":"அல்லற்","lemma":"allal","gloss":"distress"}],"gloss":"distress"},{"surface":"காலை","parts":[{"text":"காலை","lemma":"kālai","gloss":"time"}],"gloss":"time"},{"surface":"நில்லலன்","parts":[{"text":"நில்லலன்","lemma":"nillalaṉ","gloss":"he will not stand aloof"}],"gloss":"he will not stand aloof"},{"surface":"மன்னே","parts":[{"text":"மன்","lemma":"maṉ","gloss":"indeed"},{"text":"ஏ","lemma":"ē","gloss":"emphasis"}],"gloss":"indeed"}]}],"literal":"Forked ear of millet pounded cooked rice / with pollen unique street with buds abundant / wild mustard white flower white curd having mixed / cowherd woman cooked sweet and sour porridge / field beans pluckers to their fill eating / southern lord of the hills good country even within / he of Pisir they say my life protector indeed / wealthy time even if present / distress time he will not stand aloof indeed","translation":"The cooked rice of pounded, forked ears of millet, mixed with white curd and the white flowers of wild mustard that bloom abundantly with buds in the pollen-strewn streets, cooked into a sweet and sour porridge by the cowherd woman, is eaten to their fill by those who pluck field beans. Even within that good country of the southern lord of the hills, there is a man from Pisir, they say, who is indeed the protector of my life. Even if he is absent during times of wealth, he will never stand aloof during times of distress.","modern":"கிளைத்த கதிர்களைக் கொண்ட வரகினை இடித்துச் சமைத்த சோற்றோடு, மகரந்தம் நிறைந்த தெருக்களில் மொட்டுகளுடன் செழித்து வளரும் வேளையின் வெண்மையான பூக்களை வெண்தயிரோடு சேர்த்து, ஆயர் மகள் சமைத்த புளிப்பான கஞ்சியை, அவரைக்காய் பறிப்பவர்கள் வயிறார உண்ணும் தென்னகப் பாண்டிய நாட்டின் நல்ல பகுதியிலே, பிசிர் என்னும் ஊரைச் சேர்ந்தவன் என்று சொல்லப்படும் என் உயிரைக் காப்பவன் வாழ்கிறான். அவன் செல்வம் உள்ள காலத்தில் என்னோடு இல்லாவிட்டாலும், எனக்குத் துன்பம் வரும் காலத்தில் என்னைத் தனியே விட்டு விலக மாட்டான்.","explanation":"The Chola king Kōpperuñcōḻaṉ is speaking about his dear friend, the poet Picirāntaiyār, to his courtiers. Facing conflicts with his sons, the king has decided to fast unto death (vaṭakkiruttal) and is waiting for his friend, whom he has never met in person but shares a deep soul-bond with. The king describes the fertile Pandyan country where Picirāntaiyār lives, detailing the simple, rich food of the common folk, such as millet rice with curd, wild mustard flowers, and sour porridge. He asserts that Picirāntaiyār is the protector of his life. Though they might not have met during prosperous times, the king is certain his friend will arrive to be by his side in this time of ultimate distress.","model":"gemini-3.5-flash"}}